UNIT directive_spans
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 a5c85ce6a72d5e96ae2ae12844a074c05fe48a590f6eddec3163e696476774aa
SIG export default function directive_spans(text: string): Array<[number, number]>
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime: text=string (UTF-16, well-formed); i64=number (a safe integer); tuple=[number,
  number]; list=Array. STRICT: the artifact must type-check under `strict: true` against this SIG, with no `any`, no
  non-null assertions (`!`), and no `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`.
MECHANISM (restated from js; language files are self-contained) R1 = text.split with the pinned LINE_BREAK regex. R7 =
  walk the same breaks in order (matchAll of LINE_BREAK with the g flag) and advance the git line on "\n" and "\r\n",
  never on a lone "\r"; LAST = Math.max(1, text.split("\n").length minus 1 when text.endsWith("\n")). R8 = one pair per
  distinct git line.
MECHANISM R2 = replace the pinned LEAD match by itself with every U+FEFF deleted, then delete the pinned TRAIL match.
  JS \s, String.prototype.trim, trimStart and trimEnd must not realize SPACE: their set holds no-break space, U+FEFF,
  LINE SEPARATOR, U+3000 and others that are content here (R4).
MECHANISM R4 = the line up to the first index of a space or a tab; R5 and R6 = the pinned COLON_NAME and NAME regexes,
  without the i flag, and a strict comparison with "CITED". Index reads on a string under noUncheckedIndexedAccess are
  string | undefined: narrow them by comparison, never with `!`.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex LINE_BREAK = /\r\n|\r|\n/ CITED R1 R7 (alternation order puts CR LF first)
PINNED regex LEAD = /^[ \t\uFEFF]+/ CITED R2
PINNED regex TRAIL = /[ \t]+$/ CITED R2
PINNED regex COLON_NAME = /^[A-Z][A-Z0-9-]*:$/ CITED R5
PINNED regex NAME = /^[A-Z][A-Z0-9-]*$/ CITED R6
PROVENANCE rederive@9e2245be5f42 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs spans, gitLine and cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs (sirLines, parse, isDirectiveName, ATTR_ONLY), MIT.
